WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.335
scan stores eight flags in shared values.

00:00:03.335 --> 00:00:11.420
For each step, all threads finish the old stage, read a partner into previous, and reach another barrier before updating shared storage.

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:16.805
Subtracting flags[t] converts the inclusive prefix to an exclusive offset.

00:00:18.305 --> 00:00:19.790
Read old stage.

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:22.010
Keep the partner value in previous.

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:23.315
Synchronise.

00:00:23.315 --> 00:00:26.130
Finish old reads before any thread updates.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:27.565
Write new stage.

00:00:27.565 --> 00:00:30.725
Add the partner; repeat at the next distance.

00:00:32.225 --> 00:00:36.125
A shared-memory stage lets a block exchange prefix values.

00:00:36.125 --> 00:00:41.485
Registers keep the partner value separate while a barrier protects the old shared snapshot.

00:00:41.485 --> 00:00:44.705
A block barrier does not order a multi-block scan.
